    {
      "date": "2026-09-30",
      "headline": "US air defenses leave with troops, raising Kurdistan vulnerability",
      "detail": "Patriot and C-RAM air defense systems deployed at Erbil were withdrawn with personnel, removing a key interception layer for Iranian missiles and drones. KRG Prime Minister Masrour Barzani warned leaving the Kurdistan Region without air defenses is a cause for concern, citing more than 1,000 drone and ballistic missile attacks since the US-Israeli war on Iran began Feb. 28, 2026.",
      "where": "Erbil, Kurdistan Region, Iraq",
      "verification": "researched",
      "sources": [
        "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/30/how-does-iraqs-security-change-after-us-forces-withdraw",
        "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/09/08/us-air-defence-exit-from-iraq-risks-creating-wider-regional-security-gap",
        "https://www.forbes.com/sites/pauliddon/2026/09/27/why-iraqi-kurdistan-fears-looming-loss-of-us-air-defense-umbrella"
      ],
      "from": "/geopolitics/2026-10-01"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-30",
      "headline": "Sovereignty celebrations held as air-defense gap and stalled militia disarmament persist",
      "detail": "Iraq declared Sovereignty Days as a national holiday September 30 to October 3, 2026, and held military parades and convoys in Baghdad and Najaf celebrating the withdrawal. US air defenses left with troops, leaving Kurdistan without a replacement system; the Peshmerga Ministry said the region faced more than 1,000 drone and ballistic-missile attacks during the US-Iran war since February 2026 and called the departure without a defense system a cause for concern. Only a handful of less-influential militias agreed to disarm by the original September 30 deadline while powerful Iran-close groups rejected or conditioned it, prompting the extension to June 2027.",
      "where": "Baghdad and Najaf, Iraq; Erbil, Kurdistan Region",
